# htop has no theme format. color_scheme is an integer 0-6 selecting one of six
# built-ins, and there is no way to hand it hex values -- so the Lain look here
# comes from the terminal's own 16-colour ANSI mapping, which both terminals
# already define (kitty/themes/lain-theme.conf, foot's [colors-dark] regular0-7
# and bright8-15). Scheme 0 is the one that draws from those slots instead of
# hardcoding its own, so it is the only correct choice for this rice. To change
# htop's colours, change the terminal palette.
#
# htop rewrites this file on exit, saving any sort/column change made in the UI.
# Under chezmoi's symlink mode that edits the repo through the link, which is
# intended -- the same deal as nwg-look. If it ever replaces the link with a real
# file instead, it becomes live state and comes out of chezmoi's control.
